From 7e03310af8d1b5fdabf6ec2b9b54719eee9c7f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:48:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] media: rc: add keymap for the Octagon SF8008 remote

The Octagon SF8008 ships with a NEC remote control using address 0x05.
Add a keytable for it and select it from the board device trees so that
the on-SoC IR receiver reports usable key events out of the box.

Without a keymap the hix5hd2 IR receiver registers with RC_MAP_EMPTY,
which leaves no protocol enabled and maps every scancode to
KEY_RESERVED. Naming the map in the device tree also makes rc-core
enable the NEC decoder at registration time.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts  |  1 +
 .../hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts  |  1 +
 drivers/media/rc/keymaps/Makefile             |  1 +
 drivers/media/rc/keymaps/rc-octagon-sf8008.c  | 81 +++++++++++++++++++
 include/media/rc-map.h                        |  1 +
 5 files changed, 85 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/rc/keymaps/rc-octagon-sf8008.c

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
index 86ba0998659e..9c0e7d0e8b1f 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
@@ -214,6 +214,7 @@ eth_phy0: phy@3 {
 
 /* IR receiver behind the front panel window. */
 &ir {
+	linux,rc-map-name = "rc-octagon-sf8008";
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3798mv200-octagon-sf8008.dts
